-- title:
--   Admissible one-sided cost curve on $[0,\mathrm{cap})$
-- statement:
--   A one-sided cost curve $K$ with initial price $p_\star$ and capacity $\mathrm{cap}>0$ is **admissible** if $K$ is continuous, strictly increasing and convex on $[0,\mathrm{cap})$, $K(0)=0$, its right derivative at $0$ is $p_\star>0$, and $K(z)\to\infty$ as $z\uparrow\mathrm{cap}$.
--
--   These are the properties of the pool cost $C$ on $[0,x_0)$ with $p_\star=p_0$, of the extended cost $\widetilde C_M$ on $[0,M+x_0)$ and of the reverse extended cost $\widetilde C^{\rm rev}_M$ on $[0,p_0M+y_0)$ (Lemma 6.1). The one-sided auction generated by such a curve is `chordMech`.
-- source:
--   Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §6.1, Lemma 6.1, p.27 (PDF p.29); §2, p.5 (PDF p.7)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

open Filter Topology Set

namespace SybilClinch

/-- Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, *Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design*, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §6.1, Lemma 6.1, printed p.27 (PDF p.29), and §2, printed p.5 (PDF p.7): the properties of
a one-sided cost curve `K` on `[0, cap)` used by the one-sided AMM clinching auction: continuous,
strictly increasing and convex on `[0, cap)`, `K 0 = 0`, right derivative `p⋆ > 0` at `0`, and
`K z → ∞` as `z ↑ cap`.

These are the properties the paper lists for `C` on `[0, x₀)` (p.5, p.8), for `C̃_M` on
`[0, M + x₀)` and for `C̃^rev_M` on `[0, p₀M + y₀)` (Lemma 6.1).

**Formalization Note.** `K` is a total function `ℝ → ℝ`; only its values on `[0, cap)` are
constrained. The right derivative at `0` is `HasDerivWithinAt K pstar (Ici 0) 0`. -/
structure IsAdmissibleCost (K : ℝ → ℝ) (pstar cap : ℝ) : Prop where
  pstar_pos : 0 < pstar
  cap_pos : 0 < cap
  continuousOn : ContinuousOn K (Ico 0 cap)
  strictMonoOn : StrictMonoOn K (Ico 0 cap)
  convexOn : ConvexOn ℝ (Ico 0 cap) K
  zero : K 0 = 0
  rightDeriv_zero : HasDerivWithinAt K pstar (Ici 0) 0
  tendsto_cap : Tendsto K (𝓝[<] cap) atTop

end SybilClinch


